# Hall of Echoes copying a creature with counters: it "doesn't copy whether that creature ... has any counters on it" (the
# ruling, CR 707.2), and it doesn't enter, so "enters with" doesn't apply (the ruling). Bot1's Walking Ballista entered
# with one +1/+1 counter for X=1; on turn 3 the Hall becomes a copy of it - a 0/0 Walking Ballista with no counters - and
# dies to state-based actions (CR 704.5f): the Hall of Echoes card goes to the graveyard and the real Ballista stays, 1/1.

[Bot1 Deck]
Hall of Echoes
Sol Ring
Black Lotus
Walking Ballista
Plains x3
Plains x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Hall of Echoes.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Hall of Echoes.Activate(Ability: Add)
Bot1.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Walking Ballista.Cast(X: 1)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Walking Ballista.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Hall of Echoes.Activate(Bot1.Battlefield.Walking Ballista; Ability: becomes a copy)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield = Sol Ring; Walking Ballista
Bot1.Battlefield.Walking Ballista.Power = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Walking Ballista.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
Bot1.Graveyard = Hall of Echoes; Black Lotus
